          "tab_item_UWfMzX": {
            "type": "tab_item",
            "settings": {
              "tab_name": "GETTING STARTED",
              "title": "Caring for your Smithey",
              "subtitle": "Step-by-Step Guide",
              "content": "<ol><li>Use it frequently. The oil from your food keeps it healthy and builds your seasoning over time.</li><li>Clean with warm water (a few drops of dish soap won't hurt).</li><li>Dry your Smithey thoroughly to avoid rust. We sometimes put ours back on a warm burner to evaporate any excess moisture.</li><li>Oil and re-season as needed. Visit our seasoning page for more information.</li></ol>"
            }
          },
          "tab_item_DBYXGz": {
            "type": "tab_item",
            "settings": {
              "tab_name": "Cleaning",
              "title": "Cleaning your Smithey",
              "subtitle": "Step-by-Step Guide",
              "content": "<ol><li>Depending on what you've cooked, wipe your Smithey clean with a paper towel, or use warm soapy water to scrub off any excess food or oil. For tougher, stuck-on messes, use a metal spatula or chainmail scrubber to work away stubborn bits.</li><li>If you've used soap and water, make sure your Smithey is fully dry — either towel dry it or place it back on the stovetop over heat until any moisture is gone.</li><li>Add a light sheen of a neutral oil to the entire surface of your Smithey. This protects it from rust and helps maintain the seasoning.</li></ol>"
            }
          },
          "tab_item_fcnNFf": {
            "type": "tab_item",
            "settings": {
              "tab_name": "Removing Rust",
              "title": "HOW TO REMOVE RUST",
              "subtitle": "Step-by-Step Guide",
              "content": "<ol><li>Scrub the rust away using a steel wool or a chainmail scrubber and soapy water. Until all visible rust is removed.</li><li>Rinse thoroughly with warm water until the water runs clean.</li><li>Return to heat on the stovetop and dry fully.</li><li>Add a small seasoning layer to protect your Smithey's surface from future rust.</li></ol>"
            }
          }
